e they'll allow us to to  react to changes  in mutating pathogens  with tweaks to vaccines a lot more  cheaply and a lot more rapidly  and they can even be designed to attack  non-infectious diseases like cancer  so if there's a silver lining to covid19  it's it's that in the future  the mrna vaccines develop to fight it  and what they teach us will save many  many more lives  far beyond the pandemic  [Music]  here's a look at a couple of other  stories making news during this  coronavirus pandemic u.s drug maker  merck and co says its covert antiviral  pill  mole new pirava can reduce the risk of  hospitalization or death by 50 percent  that's according to findings of an  interim analysis of a late stage trial  the treatment if approved by authorities  could give doctors more tools to fight  covert  being closed for nearly 300 days beaches  in the cuban capital havana have  reopened authorities gave the green  light for resuming outdoor activities  with most of the city's residents  vaccinated against covert 19.  beaches and pools can now operate at  limited capacity along with bars and  restaurants  italy has become the first european  country to mandate covert 19 health  passes for all workers  in future employees will need to have a  so-called green pass or be suspended  from their jobs without pay  they'll also have the option of showing  a negative test which they'll have to  pay for the government hopes the measure  will see more people get vaccinated  italy's government taking tough measures  to combat covert 19. from next month it  will be mandatory for all workers in  public and private sectors to get a  health pass users will have to show  proof of vaccination a negative test or  recovery from infection  the green pass is an instrument of  freedom that makes places safer secondly  the green pass makes our vaccination  campaign more effective  on the streets of rome there's a mixed  reaction to the announcement  the green pass is an important tool to  deal